[I] Smaller, easier, more powerful, and more reliable than make

[T] redo is an implementation of Daniel J. Bernstein's redo recursive build
[T] system, aiming to be smaller, easier, more powerful and more reliable
[T] than make. This version by Avery Pennarun (apenwarr/redo) includes
[T] parallel builds, improved logging, extensive automated tests and
[T] debugging features.

[U] https://redo.readthedocs.io/en/latest/

[A] Apenwarr-redo Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS

[V] 0.42d
[L] APL

